{
 "about": [
  "What Rev4a depends on in OpenClaw, in a form scripts can check (rev4a-deps.mjs, compare.mjs, triage.mjs).",
  "It is a hand-kept subset of references/inventory.md: every entry carries the inventory id it comes from.",
  "Keep it in sync in the same commit as inventory.md: a new KR/KW key, J field, C command or I internal there gets an entry here.",
  "Each entry's `evidence` is a file and a literal text that must appear in it; scripts/test-openclaw-upgrade-scripts.mjs fails when one no longer does, so a moved touchpoint cannot leave this file stale.",
  "Config paths: `.` between keys, `[]` for array items, `<key>` for a map key. JSON paths: the snapshot shape notation (`$.jobs[].id`); `a|b` means either field is accepted.",
  "`values`: the values Rev4a writes; when the target schema has an enum there, each must still be in it.",
  "`optional`: Rev4a tolerates the field being absent, so its absence in both snapshots is not reported."
 ],
